       "| Decision Tree | 62.6% | 1.9% |\n",
       "| Gradient Boosting | 60.6% | 0.8% |\n",
       "| KNN | 57.9% | 1.0% |\n",
       "\n",
       "- **Logistic Regression** has the best test F1-score (67.3%), the best balance between precision and recall.\n",
       "- **Random Forest** has the highest recall (82.8%), so it finds the most High Potential leads.\n",
       "- **Gradient Boosting** has the highest precision (67.2%) and **Gradient Boosting** the highest accuracy (73.4%), so its High Potential predictions are the most reliable, but models like this usually miss more good leads.\n",
       "- 7 of the 7 models beat the baseline accuracy of 61.2%, and all of them find High Potential leads, which the baseline never does.\n",
       "- In cross-validation the best model is **Random Forest** (F1 66.8% +/- 1.5%). When the top models are closer to each other than this +/- value, they cannot be separated reliably.\n",
       "\n",
       "**Which model would I choose?** A wasted call on a Low Potential lead costs a little sales time, but a missed High Potential lead can cost a sale, so recall matters more here than precision. I would therefore choose **Random Forest** (best cross-validated F1) if it also has good recall in the table above, and I would only prefer the model with the highest precision if the sales team had very little time for calls.\n"
